WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.759
Week 2: Greetings and First Contact. greet and take leave introduce yourself and another person choose tú or usted

2
00:00:07.759 --> 00:00:20.855
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can greet and take leave, introduce yourself and another person, choose tú or usted. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:20.855 --> 00:00:29.275
Language system. Subject pronouns, polite versus familiar address, present-tense ser for identity, and omitted subjects.

4
00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:35.733
Sound and delivery. Link final vowels into the next word and keep unstressed vowels clear.

5
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:44.903
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:44.903 --> 00:01:07.516
Model language. Hola, me llamo Alex. — Hello, my name is Alex. Mucho gusto, señora Rivera. — Pleased to meet you, Mrs. Rivera. ¿Cómo te llamas? — What's your name? Le presento a mi compañera. — This is my colleague. Nos vemos mañana; que tenga buen día. — See you tomorrow; have a good day.

7
00:01:07.516 --> 00:01:17.265
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
